      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "In my remarks today, I will discuss inflation and its role in the Federal Reserve's conduct of monetary policy."
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Federal Reserve should try to keep inflation close to 2 percent"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Federal Reserve has not always been successful in fulfilling the price stability element of its mandate"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Large jumps in food and energy prices played a role in this upward move, but they were not the whole story"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "core inflation, the solid black line, which excludes food and energy prices, we see that it too starts to move higher in the mid-1960s"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "inflation",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": "shocks to food and energy prices",
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "the Federal Reserve was insufficiently focused on returning inflation to a predictable, low level following the shocks to food and energy prices and other disturbances"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "inflation",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "inflation came down further following the 1990-91 recession and subsequent slow recovery"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "the United States has experienced very low inflation on average since the financial crisis"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "In 2012 the FOMC adopted, for the first time, an explicit longer-run inflation objective of 2 percent"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Persistent high inflation induces households and firms to spend time and effort trying to minimize their cash holdings and forces businesses to adjust prices more frequently than"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "More importantly, high inflation also tends to raise the after-tax cost of capital, thereby discouraging business investment."
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "inflation",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Survey data suggest that this effect is probably the number one reason why people dislike inflation so much."
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "nominal federal funds rate",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": "economic downturns",
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "The FOMC fights economic downturns by reducing the nominal federal funds rate, the rate charged by banks to lend to each other overnight."
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "real federal funds rate",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "The lowest the FOMC can feasibly push the real federal funds rate is essentially the negative value of the inflation rate."
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": "monetary policy",
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Monetary Policy Actions since the Financial Crisis"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "longer-term interest rates",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "the FOMC took a variety of unprecedented actions to help lower longer-term interest rates"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "macro_economy",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "the unemployment rate, which peaked at 10 percent in 2009, is now 5.1 percent"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "the Committee expects that inflation will gradually return to 2 percent over the next two or three years"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Inflation Dynamics Models used to describe and predict inflation commonly distinguish between changes in food and energy prices--which enter into total inflation--and movements in"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "industry_supply_demand",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": "core inflation",
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Movements in certain types of input costs, particularly changes in the price of imported goods, also can cause core inflation to deviate noticeably from its trend"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": "illustrate",
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Figure 6 illustrates this point with a stylized example of the inflation consequences of a gradual increase in the level of import prices"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Such conditions--which arguably prevailed in the United States from the 1970s to the mid-1990s--could plausibly arise if the central bank has, in the past, allowed significant and "
    },
    {
      "event_type": "unknown",
      "subject": null,
      "action": null,
      "object": null,
      "key_period": null,
      "key_values": null,
      "conditions": null,
      "evidence_type": "explicit",
      "quote": "Then the response of inflation to a temporary increase in the rate of change of import prices or any other transitory shock will resemble the pattern shown in panel B"
    },
    {
      "event_type": "monetary_fiscal",
      "subject": null,
      "action": "monetary policy",
      "object": null,
